     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Is it possible to include multiple inputs under the &quot;demographics&quot; section? How do I specify them in the inputIDs? I am trying this:<div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">demographics </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    inputId </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;a&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    label </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Label&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    choices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Yes&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;No&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> selected </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;No&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  textInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    inputID </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;b&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    label </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;Free-form text&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    value </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>[…]</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">demographics_inputIDs </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div>But I get an error: <span style=\"color:rgb(255,0,0);font-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:14px\">Attribute &#39;names&#39; [2] must have the same length as the vector [1]</span></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</div></div>"
    ]
